  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (control, $[2,1,0]^2$; 2026-10-02; 200 digits, $\\varepsilon_0=10^{-8}$, extrapolation error $\\sim10^{-25}$; data about 9 s)\n- **The pipeline reproduces the analytic adjoint result exactly.** The singlet is the only contaminated state, and its fit is validated on 5 held-out $t$ to $10^{-24}$:\n  $$\\hat k_{(1,1)}=K_{(1,1)}/K_{(2,1)}=-\\frac{t-1}{2t-3},\\qquad \\rho=K_{(2,1)}/S_{(2,1)}=\\frac{2t-3}{3}.$$\n  In raw-eigenvalue normalization these are the known $K_{11}/S_{21}=-1/3$ and $K_{21}/S_{21}=(2t-3)/3$, since $f_{21}/f_{11}=t-1$. The clean combination is therefore $(2t-3)\\,d_{(1,1)}+(t-1)\\,d_{(2,1)}$, i.e. $\\beta(t)$.\n- **Already clean:** $[4,1,1]$, $[3,3,0]$ and both octets ($|\\rho|\\sim10^{-25}$).\n- **Octet multiplicity space.** The copies' signal directions satisfy $\\hat s_{(1,1),c}=A(t)+B(t)\\lambda_c$ exactly, with rational $A,B$ of degrees 3 and 1. Here $\\lambda_c$ is the copy's untwisted $t_2(2/9)$ eigenvalue, and $\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2$, $\\lambda_1\\lambda_2$ are polynomials in $t$ of degrees 2 and 4. So copy-dependent data are rational in $(t,\\lambda_c)$, as hoped.\n- **Conclusion.** The method is validated; apply it to $[3,1,0]$ (`Clean-coeffs-310-EH.wb`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
